hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1393","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) came on the night of his journey with two cups of wine and milk. He looked at them and took the milk. Gabriel (ﷺ) said: “Praise be to Allah who guided you to good nature. If you had taken wine, your nation would have gone astray” [Muslim]."
"1394","And on his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Every matter of importance that does not begin with: Praise be to Allah, it is futile and devoid of blessing.” A good hadith, [Narrated by Abu Dawud and others]."
"1395","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a servant’s son dies, Allah Almighty says to His angels: Have you taken possession of My servant’s son? They say: Yes. He says: Have you taken the fruit of his heart? They say: Yes. So he says: So what did My servant say? They say: He praised You and made istirja' (i.e., said, 'Verily we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return'). Then Allah Almighty says: Build for my servant a house in Paradise, and call it the House of Praise.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"1396","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Allah is pleased with His slave who says: 'Al-hamdu lillah (praise be to Allah)' when he takes a morsel of food and drinks a draught of water."" [Muslim] ."
